# The Hub team owns this repo. A PR requests their review automatically
# (a draft PR requests it when it is marked ready).
*  @camunda/hub

# The engine and the camunda-oca config also build OCA's tests, and the test automation team stays
# responsible for OCA. A PR touching them requests both teams; either one can review.
/semantic-graph-extractor/  @camunda/hub @camunda/test-automation-team
/path-analyser/             @camunda/hub @camunda/test-automation-team
/materializer/              @camunda/hub @camunda/test-automation-team
/request-validation/        @camunda/hub @camunda/test-automation-team
/emitter-sdk/               @camunda/hub @camunda/test-automation-team
/configs/camunda-oca/       @camunda/hub @camunda/test-automation-team

# The camunda-oca spec-pin bump (the chore/spec-bump-camunda-oca PR) is OCA's own concern, so it goes
# to the test automation team only — not the Hub team. More specific than the rule above, so it
# wins (CODEOWNERS is last-match-wins).
/configs/camunda-oca/spec-pin.json  @camunda/test-automation-team
